    "body": "@ptoomey3 it's similar to the body being sent there if you use 307/308 (or 301/302 with a method that is not POST). In general the server receiving all the secrets could relay them if they want.\r\n\r\nThe threat model here seems to be that the server is cooperating but has an XSS of sorts around its `Location` header handling. I suppose another solution here could be to introduce a new redirect mode, whereby you can only redirect within the origins provided by the request URL and yourself, or some such. (That would also address the request body issue, potential issues with secrets in the request method, etc.)",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
